[rvn-ple] Fail closed on a manifest encoder_version other than the frozen r1

parse_manifest only checked that encoder_version was a non-empty string, so a
checkpoint produced by a different encoder build -- one renamed by a later
schema revision, or a tampered ple_storage.json -- loaded silently and served.
The offline gate already refuses every other producer version against the
frozen literal "rvn-ple-nvfp4-r1" (tools/rvn_ple/verify.py ENCODER_VERSION,
schema section 2), so the runtime must not bless what the verifier rejected:
compare for exact equality and raise naming both the observed and the frozen
expected value, exactly like the format_version and required_loader_feature
checks beside it.

--- a/python/sglang/srt/models/rvn_ple_storage.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/models/rvn_ple_storage.py
@@ -20,6 +20,10 @@
 MANIFEST_NAME = "ple_storage.json"
 FORMAT_VERSION = 1
 REQUIRED_LOADER_FEATURE = "ple-packed-nvfp4-v1"
+# Schema §2: the only encoder build whose output this loader may decode; the
+# offline gate (tools/rvn_ple/verify.py) refuses every other producer version
+# with this exact frozen literal, and the loader now refuses them too.
+ENCODER_VERSION = "rvn-ple-nvfp4-r1"
 WEIGHT_DTYPE = "e2m1-packed-u8-low-first"
 SCALE_DTYPE = "float8_e4m3fn"
 GROUP_SIZE = 16
@@ -168,6 +172,11 @@
            "not fall back")
     encoder_version = raw["encoder_version"]
     _string(encoder_version, "encoder_version")
+    _check(encoder_version == ENCODER_VERSION,
+           f"unsupported encoder_version {encoder_version!r}; this loader "
+           f"only decodes tables produced by {ENCODER_VERSION!r} (schema "
+           "section 2, the same frozen value the offline verifier enforces) "
+           "and does not fall back")
 
     source = raw["source"]
     _check(isinstance(source, dict) and set(source) == _SOURCE_KEYS,
